/*
 * Phase 2k.2: gram.lime is now the authoritative source for the backend
 * SQL grammar.  This .y file is kept ONLY because ecpg's parse.pl reads
 * it to generate preproc.y.  When you edit the grammar:
 *   1. Edit this file (gram.y) -- it remains human-readable bison form.
 *   2. Run: python3 src/tools/lime_convert_gram.py \
 *              src/backend/parser/gram.y src/backend/parser/gram.lime
 *   3. Hand-merge any new C code in the post-%% epilogue into the
 *      epilogue %include block at the end of gram.lime.
 *   4. Commit both files together.
 * Phase 2k.3 (follow-up) will rewrite parse.pl to consume gram.lime
 * directly so this dual-tracking goes away.
 */

